What is under which licence
---------------------------

AGPL-3.0-only (LICENSE) — the database: everything in this repository not
listed below, among it crates/ (but the three below), editions/,
modules/, playground/, bench/, fuzz/, integrations/, scripts/.

MIT (the LICENSE file in each directory) — what programs use to reach
the database, so that any program, open or closed, can:

  drivers/          the drivers (C, C++, Java, JavaScript/TypeScript,
                    Python, Swift, Android) — their source
  crates/client/    the Rust driver, and what it is built from:
  crates/wire/      the protocol's wire format
  crates/crypto/    the hashes and SCRAM it authenticates with
  examples/         the examples, to copy from

The database itself, where a driver's package carries it — the embedded
edition's library in the Python wheel, drivers/js/wasm/nucleus.wasm in
the npm package, its Node addon, NucleusEmbedded.xcframework for Swift,
the Android library's native libraries — stays under AGPL-3.0-only (such a
package is "MIT AND AGPL-3.0-only").  A program that talks to a nucleus
server through a driver is not a work based on the database; a program
that opens a database in its own process with the embedded edition is.

Network use (AGPL section 13): whoever runs a modified database for users
who reach it over a network must offer those users its source — the
version they run, with the changes.  Running it unmodified, or reaching it
through the drivers, asks nothing more.

